diff --git a/memory/note/n_1010_828f.md b/memory/note/n_1010_828f.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..c0c5762d8c
--- /dev/null
+++ b/memory/note/n_1010_828f.md
@@ -0,0 +1,22 @@
+---
+id: "n_1010_828f"
+type: "note"
+title: "gh-1801 fix (2026-10-23): the release train's empty-latest-release creators were auto_release.sh (`gh release create --latest` with ZERO assets on every main-push train — the fa update 404 window) plus asset-less lazy creates in ci.yml binaries/web-spa and build-macos.yml CLI/extension jobs. Fixed by removing the auto_release create entirely (binaries job owns creation) and making every lazy create DRAFT-first with `--draft=false --latest` only in steps that upload a real fa-*.tar.gz/zip; release_attach_or_create.sh's attach path now publishes drafts too. Invariant pinned by test/release_empty_latest_guard_test.dart (no release may become latest without a CLI asset). FORENSICS LESSON from the same ticket: the filed \"mobile legs cancel each other via shared concurrency\" was WRONG — build-mobile run 39905802767 was killed by its OWN 90m build-ios job ceiling (check-run annotation \"exceeded the maximum execution time\"), the sibling had finished 78 min earlier, and the #351 group is per-run_id with cancel-in-progress:false; ALSO the job declared runs-on [self-hosted, macos-m5, fa-m5-1] yet executed on fa-m5-2, so that runner carries a stale fa-m5-1 label in GitHub runner settings (repo code cannot fix; gh-1692 routing contract). Before blaming concurrency for a \"cancelled\" run: check the job's check-run annotations (timeout kills report conclusion=cancelled) and compare the sibling's completion time."
+author: "agent"
+date: "2026-10-23T10:00:53.579603Z"
+area: "project"
+topics: []
+source: "agent"
+accessCount: 0
+importance: 0.5
+tags: ["#note", "#source_agent", "ci", "workflows", "release", "gh-1801", "concurrency", "fa-update", "root-cause", "self-hosted-runner"]
+---
+
+
+# Note: n_1010_828f
+
+gh-1801 fix (2026-10-23): the release train's empty-latest-release creators were auto_release.sh (`gh release create --latest` with ZERO assets on every main-push train — the fa update 404 window) plus asset-less lazy creates in ci.yml binaries/web-spa and build-macos.yml CLI/extension jobs. Fixed by removing the auto_release create entirely (binaries job owns creation) and making every lazy create DRAFT-first with `--draft=false --latest` only in steps that upload a real fa-*.tar.gz/zip; release_attach_or_create.sh's attach path now publishes drafts too. Invariant pinned by test/release_empty_latest_guard_test.dart (no release may become latest without a CLI asset). FORENSICS LESSON from the same ticket: the filed "mobile legs cancel each other via shared concurrency" was WRONG — build-mobile run 39905802767 was killed by its OWN 90m build-ios job ceiling (check-run annotation "exceeded the maximum execution time"), the sibling had finished 78 min earlier, and the #351 group is per-run_id with cancel-in-progress:false; ALSO the job declared runs-on [self-hosted, macos-m5, fa-m5-1] yet executed on fa-m5-2, so that runner carries a stale fa-m5-1 label in GitHub runner settings (repo code cannot fix; gh-1692 routing contract). Before blaming concurrency for a "cancelled" run: check the job's check-run annotations (timeout kills report conclusion=cancelled) and compare the sibling's completion time.
+
+**By:** [[agent]]
+**Date:** 2026-10-23T10:00:53.579603Z
+**Area:** [[project|project]]
